116 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 87 0 R
/E (The purpose of the Git-CLI-Scanner is to perform automatic scans of Git repositories in order to detect potentially sensitive information that might have been committed by mistake. It is used to help find credentials, API keys, tokens, passwords, configuration files, and other data that can pose a potential security risk if they get into the wrong hands. The scanner allows scanning of Git repositories for secrets using predefined rules and detecting potentially sensitive data that may be present in the history of changes even if it is no longer present in the current version of the code. It aims to prevent human error, ensure repository security, facilitate secure coding practices, and raise awareness of data exposure risks.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
