132 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 89 0 R
/E (The Git-CLI-Scanner is designed as an automated utility that scans a repository for possible exposed secrets. First, it needs to be initialized by a user who inputs a particular command in the command line in which the tool should be launched. The repository path is specified in the command line by the user. The tool checks the repository and lists all files and folders to be scanned. The files that are irrelevant, ignored, or contain binary data are excluded from the scan. Then, the contents of the relevant files are read, and matching rules, patterns, and keywords are applied. The tool helps detect hardcoded credentials, API keys, tokens, passwords, configuration data, or other values that should not be stored in the repository. For improved accuracy, the scanning tool analyzes the context around the matched patterns and uses entropy to spot secrets-like values with high probability.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
