157 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 91 0 R
/E (The Git-CLI-Scanner has a lot of valuable capabilities for analyzing the security of Git repositories. One of its key capabilities is its ability to automate the scanning of the source code and configuration files for the purpose of identifying sensitive information according to certain pre-defined rules and pattern matching. The scanner is able to detect any suspicious credentials, passwords, access tokens, etc. It can scan the history of Git commits in order to find out if there are any potentially leaked data. The scanner is highly capable of filtering files, as well as excluding certain directories, analyzing the context of the found strings, analyzing entropy of random strings, filtering out some false positives, eliminating duplicates, and classifying the severity of detection. The scanner masks or redacts sensitive information in its output and generates a structured report, showing all necessary information.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
